  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with 64 bars in a ring, drawn as a single `instances.box` node on a floor plane. The code typechecks, but I couldn't build or run it here, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Bar heights:** `setInstances` updates them every frame from a mix of four sine waves.\n- **Colours:** each bar gets a hex colour from a hue gradient around the ring. I converted HSL to hex myself because the docs say `hsl()` strings aren't parsed.\n- **Lighting:** a neutral environment, a hemisphere light, a shadow-casting directional key light, a point light and light fog.\n- **Camera:** `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate: 0.18` orbits the ring.\n- **Ready flag:** the engine's own loop does the rendering. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` plus two animation frames.\n\nI assumed the `rotation` field is in radians, which I couldn't confirm in the docs. It only turns the square bars to face outward, so a wrong unit would be a small visual flaw.\n\n",
